flow into your web application. It includes Google Cloud Console configuration, frontend button mounting, backend

token verification, database schema design, and ready-to-use AI prompts.

2. Google Cloud Console Configuration

Navigate to Google Cloud Console (console.cloud.google.com).

Create a new project or select an existing one.

Go to APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen, select External, and complete app details.

Go to Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID.

Select Web application as the application type.

Configure the origin and callback URLs carefully:

Authorized JavaScript Origins: http://localhost:4321 (Dev), https://yourdomain.com (Prod)

Authorized Redirect URIs: http://localhost:4321/api/auth/callback/google

Save the generated Client ID and Client Secret into your .env file.

